# Default: treat every file as text and normalize to LF in the repository AND
# the working tree. With core.autocrlf=true this silences the "LF will be
# replaced by CRLF" warnings and keeps line endings deterministic across
# Windows, Linux and CI. Binaries are auto-detected and skipped. More specific
# rules below override this.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must stay LF: CRLF makes bash fail with "$'\r': command not
# found". This repository's primary development platform is Windows and its
# container jobs run these scripts inside Linux images, so this rule is
# load-bearing, not cosmetic.
*.sh text eol=lf

# V1 additionally pins its SSH deploy key and PEM files to -text, because
# core.autocrlf would rewrite them to CRLF on checkout and break OpenSSH. V2
# carries no deploy key and no remote host (see docs/SPEC.md §42 and this
# change's proposal), so those rules have nothing to protect here. The change
# that adds deployment reintroduces them with the keys they guard.
